## Original Content
President Donald Trump disclosed just over 1,000 financial transactions in the month of June in what appears to be broad reshuffling of his portfolio.

## Summary
In June, President Donald Trump disclosed over 1,000 financial transactions, indicating a significant reshuffling of his investment portfolio. This includes selling shares in companies like Meta and purchasing shares in Berkshire Hathaway.

## Key Points
- Trump disclosed over 1,000 financial transactions in June.
- Transactions involved selling stocks such as Meta and buying Berkshire Hathaway.
- This represents a broad reshuffling of his investment portfolio.


